  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.5: Root-cause fix for Avalonia table-column collapse with row-spans (#26). The v1.0.4 cap alone was not enough: weight computation didn't track row-span occupancy, so cells in continuation rows were attributed to the wrong columns, and long-prose content's weight landed on the wrong column entirely. `TableColumnWeights.Compute` now mirrors the renderer's `occupied[]` placement logic. A new `ComputeMinWidthsPixels` adds a per-column min-width floor (longest single word × ~7.5 px) wired into `ColumnDefinition.MinWidth`, so narrow header-only columns no longer collapse to one letter per line when sharing a viewport with prose columns. See CHANGELOG.md.",
